      "message": "This might be out of scope, but I don\u0027t really know. I don\u0027t see that access to last_result (via this function and usb_retimer_fw_update_get_result) is explicitly synchronized. Maybe it is effectively synchronized by thread priority.\n\nIf there is a race window between writing to last_result and reading it, it seems like this CL potentially makes the window longer. How does the reader of last_result know that the value applies to the most recently executed operation?\n\nIf this is a real issue, you might be able to avoid it by moving the wait loop into usb_retime_fw_update_get_result, which is called by a host command. It could block until the value of last_result is meaningful, assuming that wouldn\u0027t be too terribly long for the AP.",
